# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the CTest suite of a -DENABLE_THREAD_SANITIZER=ON
# build. CMake points TSAN_OPTIONS at this file for every registered test, so a
# plain `ctest --test-dir <build>` uses it without being told to.
#
# There is exactly one thing suppressed here, and it is a data race the library
# is built around rather than one it has yet to answer.
#
# When no usable time source exists, the Jitter RNG makes one: a thread that
# does nothing but increment a counter, which the collector reads as its clock.
# The increment and the read are deliberately unsynchronized - the counter is
# the noise source, and its value is meant to depend on how the two threads
# happen to interleave on this machine at this moment. Ordering the access
# would order exactly what is being measured, so this is not a race to be
# fixed; an atomic counter here would be a slower counter measuring less.
#
# The same holds for the flag that stops that thread: it is written once by the
# collector and polled by the counting thread, and the only cost of the poll
# seeing it late is one more turn of a loop that is already unbounded.
#
# Everything else the library shares between threads is a latch or a memo and
# goes through arch/jitterentropy-arch-atomic.h. Those are not suppressed, and
# tests/unit/unit-concurrency.c exists to race them: a report from it is a
# regression, which is the whole point of keeping this list to the two entries
# below.
race:jent_notime_sample_timer
race:jent_notime_unsettick
